<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Avaldsnes</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Avaldsnes is a historic site on the island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karmoy">Karmøy</a> in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a>, overlooking the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karmsund">Karmsund</a> strait. Its great burial mounds and ship burials show that powerful kings controlled the shipping lane there from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a>, and the sagas make it a royal seat of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harald-fairhair">Harald Fairhair</a>. Its stone church of St Olaf dates from about 1250.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/avaldsnes.jpg" alt="Avaldsnes" width="320" height="220" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Johan Christian Dahl · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dahl.I.C.1820.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
